# The product revision CI Gate checks each machinery wheel against: the
# installed-wheel job of ci-gate.yml checks out learn-ukrainian/
# learn-ukrainian.github.io at `commit`, collects its tests with the release
# cut's consumer_collection step and runs the `test` files below, all with
# the wheel built from the tested head first on the path.
#
# Bump deliberately, never to "latest main": pick a product main commit whose
# CI Gate succeeded, set `commit` to its full SHA, check that every `test`
# path still exists there (move or replace one the product moved), and land it
# as its own PR. That PR's CI run is the proof that the bump collects and
# passes. A product change that needs a newer machinery release is not a
# reason to bump past that release's adoption.
#
# Pinned 2026-11-17: product main f8d6e7c0. Its tree matches product #13170
# head ec3ebcff, whose CI Gate succeeded.
commit f8d6e7c08e4fe9452f3579b92a4c6ce459af7b74
# Key consumer tests: product tests that run the installed lu-machinery at
# runtime across the seams collection only imports.
test tests/api/test_installed_monitor_drill_routes.py
test tests/test_launcher_installed_helper_chain.py
test tests/review/test_product_hooks.py
